voltage               package:AA               R Documentation

Test Results of Voltage Regulators for Automobiles

Description:

     The 'voltage' data frame has 256 rows and 4 columns.

     A regulator selected randomly from the production line was
     adjusted  at one of a number of setting stations, and then tested
     at each of  four testing stations, giving the data set.

Usage:

     data(voltage)

Format:

     This data frame contains the following columns:

     'Set' a factor variable for the setting station;

     'Reg' a factor variable giving the regulator number;

     'Test' a factor variable for the testing station;

     'y' the response variable for each test.

Source:

     The data were obtained from

     Cox, D.R. and Snell, E.J. (1981),  _Applied Statistics: Principles
     and Examples_.  Chapman & Hall, London.  Page 140.

References:

     Brazzale, A.R., Davison, A.C. and Reid, N. (2007).  _Applied 
     Asymptotics: Case Studies in Small-Sample Statistics_.  Cambridge 
     University Press, Cambridge.  Example 7.3.

Examples:

     data(voltage)
     par(mfrow = c(1,3))
     boxplot(y ~ Set, data = voltage, main="setting station")
     boxplot(y ~ Test, data = voltage, main="testing station")
     boxplot(y ~ Reg, data = voltage, main="regulator number")
